LEGAL-SUITE
Copyright (c) 2026 Hrvoje Matej. All rights reserved.

1. OWNERSHIP

This is proprietary software. The code, document templates, clause texts, data
tables and documentation are copyrighted works of the rights holder. GitHub
publication is not open source licensing and grants no rights beyond section 2.

2. WHAT IS PERMITTED

You may read and review the code for inspection and assessment, for example as
an employer or reviewer, and you may fork the repository within GitHub using
GitHub's fork function for the same purpose, as GitHub's terms provide.

Without prior written permission of the rights holder you may not use the code
or templates in other projects, copy them outside GitHub, modify, distribute,
make them publicly available, sell them, provide services to third parties, or
systematically extract a substantial part of the template and data collection.

3. THE OUTPUT IS NOT LEGAL ADVICE

The application deterministically fills prepared forms with data entered by
the user. It does not assess the case and does not predict any outcome.

A generated document is not legal advice or a legal opinion and is not a
substitute for a lawyer. Use of the application creates no attorney-client
relationship. Deadlines, jurisdiction, legal basis and the content of any
submission remain the user's responsibility, and review by a lawyer before
filing is recommended (Croatian Bar Association, www.hok-cba.hr).

4. NO WARRANTY

The software and all generated documents are provided as is, without warranty
of any kind, express or implied. No warranty is given as to fitness for a
particular purpose, accuracy, completeness, legal correctness, timeliness,
compliance with regulations, or acceptance of a document by a court or public
authority. Legislation, fees and forms change, and the contents of this
repository may be out of date.

5. LIABILITY

To the extent permitted by law, the rights holder is not liable for damage
arising from use of the software or of generated documents, including a lost
case, a missed deadline, a rejected submission, costs of proceedings and lost
profit.

This limitation does not affect mandatory law. Under Croatian law, liability
for damage caused intentionally or by gross negligence cannot be excluded or
limited in advance, and this licence does not purport to exclude it. The same
applies to liability for death or personal injury and to consumer rights.

6. GOVERNING LAW

Croatian law applies, with jurisdiction of the competent court in Zagreb.
Permission requests: GitHub profile of the rights holder (hm53-byte).
